Let $	ext{mod}$ denote the modulo operation. Consider a binary vector $ {x} \in \mathbb{Z}^d_2$ which is projected as $f( {x}) =  {U}^	op  {x} 	ext{ mod } 2$ with a random binary projection matrix $\mathbb{R} \in \{0,1\}^{d 	imes p}$, where $p = O(\ln(n) / \epsilon^2)$ (usually $p \ll d$). The elements of $ {U}$ are i.i.d. with Bernoulli distribution having probability $\xi = (\epsilon^2 / \ell)$ to be one and probability $(1-\xi)$ to be zero. We have:  egin{align} & 	ext{if }\,\, \| {x}_i -  {x}_j\|_H <  rac{\ell}{4} 
onumber\ &\quad\quad\quad\implies \|f( {x}_i) - f( {x}_j)\|_H < (1+\epsilon)p\,\xi\, rac{\ell}{4}, \ & 	ext{if }\,\,  rac{\ell}{4} \leq \| {x}_i -  {x}_j\|_H \leq  rac{\ell}{2\epsilon} 
onumber\ &\implies (1-\epsilon)p\,\xi\leq rac{\|f( {x}_i) - f( {x}_j)\|_H}{\| {x}_i -  {x}_j\|_H} < (1+\epsilon)p\,\xi, \ & 	ext{if }\,\, \| {x}_i -  {x}_j\|_H >  rac{\ell}{2\epsilon} 
onumber\ &\quad\quad\quad\implies \|f( {x}_i) - f( {x}_j)\|_H > (1-\epsilon)p\,\xi\, rac{\ell}{2\epsilon}, \end{align} for all $ {x}_i,  {x}_j \in \mathbb{Z}^d_2$, with probability at least $(1-e^{-c \epsilon^4 p})$ where $c$ is a positive constant.
